# Mission — a pointer

> ⛔ **This is a pointer, not a document. Do not write product truth here.**

What {{product.name}} is — who it is for, what it does, the binding principles, what it is NOT, the promises
asserted by tests and the scorecard — lives in **one** place for every code repo:

**`.claude/context/constitution.md`** in the **`{{hub.name}}`** repository{{#hub.github}} (`{{hub.github}}`){{/hub.github}}.

## Why this file is empty

A mission statement copied into each repo is edited in one and not the others, and then nobody knows which
is true. The constitution is written once, in the hub, and beats the code everywhere. If this service
behaves differently from what it says, that is a defect in the service — not an update to reality.

